= Appendix E — Practical Checklist

== E.1 Everyday prevention

+ Wash hands with soap and clean running water at key times, including before food and after using the toilet.
+ Use safe water and clean utensils; separate raw from ready-to-eat foods.
+ Check food labels and storage instructions, including the amount per serving.
+ Follow current local guidance on vaccination and infection prevention.
+ Check the source, date and evidence behind a health claim.

== E.2 Safety and support

+ Check for scene hazards before helping; call local emergency services for severe conditions.
+ Follow dispatcher instructions and act within first-aid training.
+ Do not force food or drink into an unresponsive person's mouth.
+ Listen respectfully, protect privacy and seek appropriate help when safety is at risk.
+ Ask qualified professionals about individual treatment, symptoms and reproductive-health choices.

This checklist is educational, not a substitute for a first-aid course or individual clinical care.
